## Implemented route and player decision

Preserve a dry dash landing through the committed arm/foot patch, then use ordinary close-range primary on the actual recovering low housing/tool mount. The visible giant foot has no HP, target group or primary requirement. One local limb supplies four finite opportunities: isolated demo, apron combination, left pocket, right pocket. Six required HP30 actors are the village Scout, yard Handler, apron Handler, crossing Scout, shelter Scout and shelter Handler. No padded waves, Tender, extra boss, pickup, permanent-stat reward, damaging weed, swimming, boat, jump, narrow plank, crowd blocker or escort objective is added.

Continuous dry topY0 floor spans X±3.4 and Z[-39,3.6], with four broad staticBox supports overlapping1m: village → lock apron → grounded crossing → sheltered courtyard. Water, rails, masonry, carts and witnesses remain outboard. Exact stage order is `village → yard → yard_exit → foot_demo → apron_pair → before_crossing → crossing_left → crossing_right → far_apron → before_shelter → shelter_pair → clear`.

| Authored actor ID | Station X/Z | Role |
| --- | --- | --- |
| `village_scout` | 0/-0.5 | Ray Scout |
| `yard_handler` | 0.5/-5.7 | Salvage Handler |
| `apron_handler` | -0.45/-15.2 | Salvage Handler with apron foot |
| `crossing_scout` | 0.45/-23.5 | Ray Scout with alternating foot pockets |
| `shelter_scout` | -0.6/-33.0 | Final mixed pair |
| `shelter_handler` | 0.65/-35.2 | Final mixed pair |

Four checkpoints require an actual sampled completed dash crossing the contact region, followed by a stable response. They never require an endpoint to remain in the thin strip or heal resources.

| Contact beat | Checkpoint ID | X/Z contact bounds |
| --- | --- | --- |
| `yard_exit` | `weybridge-yard-exit` | X[-2.8,2.8], Z[-8.2,-7.1] |
| `before_crossing` | `weybridge-before-crossing` | X[-2.8,2.8], Z[-18.0,-16.9] |
| `far_apron` | `weybridge-far-apron` | X[-2.8,2.8], Z[-29.3,-28.2] |
| `before_shelter` | `weybridge-before-shelter` | X[-2.8,2.8], Z[-31.2,-30.1] |

All six actual defeats and four completed foot opportunities earn once-only completion `weybridge-crossing-clear`. Actual separate shelter contact `weybridge-shelter`, X[-2.7,2.7]/Z[-38.8,-37.5], then exits toward canonical A2-L3. Harmless distant artillery collapse begins on clear and does not delay the open exit for a decorative clock.

## Current encounter and saved-state guards

One shared Scheduler composes the reused Ray exchange with three actual stationary Handler lane mechanisms and four actual true-circle foot mechanisms. Handler roots are anchored, retain inherited accepted-hit/once-defeat/reload-credit/damage gates, and use their own five-support rig. Tools point fixed+Z with reach3.8m/radius.31. Each foot circle has radius1.10m, enclosing the1.62×1.36m visible sole corners. Stations are `foot_demo`[-.25,-10.5], `foot_apron`[.30,-13.2], `foot_left`[-.75,-21.0], `foot_right`[.75,-24.6]. Only one local foot is visible/current at a time.

| Immutable raw role | Damage | Windup / lock / active / recovery / interval seconds | HP / movement |
| --- | --- | --- | --- |
| Ray Scout | 10 | 1.55 /1.10 /.16 /1.60 /1.60 | 30 /0 |
| Handler tool | 10 | 2.20 /1.10 /.20 /1.90 /1.90 | Actor30 /0 |
| Demo/apron foot | 4 | 2.20 /1.10 /.20 /1.60 /1.80 | No target HP /0 |
| Crossing foot | 4 | 1.75 /1.10 /.20 /1.60 /1.80 | No target HP /0 |

The shared resolver applies the fixed `assisted`/`standard`/`challenge` profile; raw data and explicit timing floors retain the full1.10 lock. Cosmetics never shorten damage deadlines or alter dash distance. Crossing candidate order prefers the actual low mount while shared floor/collision/combined-threat proof remains authoritative. A paired foot uses the living actor's actual stationary opening, and its ordinary-primary start/full completion must fit that real target's retained recovery. If the Scout naturally finishes only after the whole promised response and while the foot is already withdrawing, the level retains that completed armed receipt and holds the next Scout activation until the foot finishes. It never extends danger or a recovery deadline. Earlier lost custody or actual target defeat cancels the coupled cycle. Assisted budget1 explicitly requires the real counterpart defeat before its foot opportunity, with the same six defeats/four feet/four contacts required.

Local schema1 composes sequence, actors, Scheduler, Ray and mechanism snapshots; a genuine shared unresolved path uses nested mechanism schema2 and drains back to schema1. Full saved-player preflight precedes mutation. Nested types/schemas validate before crosschecks; Handler pose/progress must match the exact saved tool clock. Defeat HP must match the earned sequence; future tools/feet remain unstarted; earned feet require an actual completed cycle receipt. Each running view retains seven fields, including canonical admission `equipment_ids`, full primary cadence, reachable supported landing/attack points and actual counterpart custody. ExactJson retains copied scalar bits/types; no clock tolerance or manufactured proof replaces authority.

Quiet commit applies player first through the shell, then actors → Scheduler → consumers → derived poses/scenery/cues. Public consumer state/hit callbacks finish actual cosmetics quietly before deferred aggregate capture, including a synchronous active-publication pause and a resumed hit-publication pause. The supported synchronous `hero.died` barrier cancels only running mechanisms/Rays with `hero_defeated`, keeps completed foot receipts and original cooldown/history, clears transient views/proofs and commits final idle cosmetics through the owned Weybridge Scout adapter inherited by Handler. Shell pause is synchronous; capture drain is deferred. Pending earned checkpoint/completion tails can be saved without requesting new progression from a corpse. Derived opacity remains unsaved presentation, with no collision, clock or damage authority.

